--allman false
--redundanttype inferred
--disable andOperator
--disable unusedArguments
--disable opaqueGenericParameters
--disable conditionalAssignment
# swiftTestingTestCaseNames (SwiftFormat 0.61+) rewrites
# `@Test("desc") func camelCase()` into `@Test func ` followed by
# the description as a backtick-quoted identifier. Those rewritten
# names then violate SwiftLint's `identifier_name` rule (capitalised
# leading char, spaces). Keep the description-string form until
# both tools agree.
--disable swiftTestingTestCaseNames
# SwiftFormat deprecated the opt-in `wrapConditionalBodies` and split it
# into per-statement rules, of which these two ship enabled by default.
# They rewrite every `if foo { return bar }` in the package onto three
# lines — 1446 sites, against a house style that deliberately keeps short
# conditional bodies inline (`if case let .chord(c) = e { return … }`).
# Disabling them is what keeps the formatter a no-op on existing code;
# without it the first pre-commit run reformats the whole repository.
--disable wrapIfStatementBodies
--disable wrapIfExpressionBodies
--lineaftermarks false
--swiftversion 6.2
--wraparguments before-first
--wrapcollections before-first
--wrapparameters before-first
--xcodeindentation enabled
--extensionacl on-declarations
